OL,3,GNEWSAScreening and jab 'gold standard'
OL,4,Ain cancer fight
OL,5,
OL,6,FWomen should keep up with cervical
OL,7,Fscreening appointments even if they
OL,8,Fhave been vaccinated, according to a
OL,9,Fchief nurse.
OL,11,FNHS Shropshire, Telford and Wrekin
OL,12,Fchief nursing officer Vanessa Whatley
OL,13,Fsaid there was a "misconception" that
OL,14,Fthe HPV vaccine offered in schools
OL,15,Fsince 2008 had replaced the need for
OL,16,Ftesting for younger women.
OL,18,FNHS figures show 72.2% of women in the
OL,19,Fcounty aged between 25 and 49 take up
OL,20,Ftheir appointments, rising to 76.3% of
OL,21,F50 to 64 year-olds. The national target
OL,22,Fis 80%.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,358,350,200,160,0,100
